      "text": "The circuit has no measurement instructions, so the classical register is never written and every shot reads back as `'000'`. Adding a measurement of all qubits into the matching classical bits fixes this.\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport qiskit\nfrom qiskit import *\n\nnumber_of_qubits = 3\nbackend_sim = Aer.get_backend('qasm_simulator')\n\ninput_circuit = QuantumCircuit(number_of_qubits, number_of_qubits)\ninput_circuit.x(0)\ninput_circuit.h(1)\ninput_circuit.cx(0,1)\ninput_circuit.i(1)\ninput_circuit.x(1)\n# FIX: circuit had no measurement, so the classical register stayed 0 and every shot returned '000' -> added measure of all qubits into the matching classical bits, because get_counts only reports values stored in classical bits\ninput_circuit.measure(range(number_of_qubits), range(number_of_qubits))\n\njob_sim = execute(input_circuit, backend_sim, shots=1024)\nresult_sim = job_sim.result()\ncounts = result_sim.get_counts(input_circuit)\nprint(counts)\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
